 "notes": "The list starts on n41.jpg (printed p. 34) and ends at the top of n42.jpg (p. 35), under the running head \"EAST COAST OF ENGLAND.\" n40.jpg (p. 33) has only the section's introduction, and the list ends before n43.jpg, so I didn't open n43.\n\nTypography: \"L.H.\" and \"L.V.\" are printed in small capitals. I've written them as \"L.H.\"/\"L.V.\" The leader dots in \"printed\" are approximate, and an empty keeper column is shown by leader dots alone. There are no map numbers, no light characters and no sub-headings. The only coast heading is the section/running head \"EAST COAST OF ENGLAND\", and the two Channel Islands stations (Casquets, Hanois) are listed under it too.\n\nFootnote: the † after Longstone L.H. refers to the footnote at the bottom of p. 34: \"† For nature of light, position, and distance from the nearest land, see Report for 1880.\" In the \"printed\" field I've put the dagger after \"L.H.\", where it stands. A small stray mark after \"Winterton L.H.\" looks like a printing blemish, so I left it out.\n\nCounts: there are 25 starred stations, which matches the introduction's \"returns have been received from twenty-five\". The list has 37 rows: 35 English stations plus Casquets and Hanois. The introduction on p. 33 says schedules went to \"thirty-seven lighthouses and light-vessels on the East Coast of England, and two stations in the Channel Islands\", which would make 39. Either the list leaves out two stations or the 37 already includes the Channel Islands.\n\nSpellings copied as printed (not errors in my reading):\n- \"Llyn Wells\" is the Lynn Well light-vessel.\n- \"Languard Point\" is usually Landguard Point.\n- \"Hasbro'\" is Happisburgh. It appears twice, once as L.H. and once as L.V.\n- \"Orfordness\" is printed as one word.\n- \"Spurn (Newsand) L.V.\" has a bracketed qualifier, which I kept as part of the name.\n- \"Edward le Gallais\" has a lower-case \"le\".\n- \"C. Prefrement\" (Cockle L.V.) may be a misprint for a surname such as Prefement or Prevement, but I've left it as printed.\n\nKeepers:\n- Shipwash and Galloper give \"The Principal\" (the master of the light-vessel) instead of a personal name. I put it in keepers as printed.\n- At Galloper, the rest of the entry (\": two batches of wings from Mr. Gurney.\", which runs onto a second line) is in other.\n- At Hasbro' L.H. the return came \"By Mr. Gurney from G. H. Dunsford.\". G. H. Dunsford is the observer. Mr. Gurney (J. H. Gurney, jun., who identified the wings) is not a keeper, so \"By Mr. Gurney from\" is in other.\n- Pairs joined by \"&\" are kept as one entry.\n\nOCR checks: the OCR's \"Spurn Giléwiend\" is \"Spurn (Newsand)\", its \"South Sand\" is \"South Sand Head\", and its \"Hastside\" is \"Eastside\".",
